This is a very good question, and the order does matter 👍
✅ Correct order (THIS IS IMPORTANT)
🥇 FIRST → CSS (blue container + button styles)
This must come before the button is rendered, so Streamlit knows how to style it.
Copy code
Python
st.markdown("""
<style>
/* Blue toggle container */
.history-toggle {
    position: fixed;
    top: 120px;
    left: 10px;
    z-index: 1000;
    background-color: #1f77b4;
    padding: 6px;
    border-radius: 8px;
}

/* Style the Streamlit button */
.history-toggle div[data-testid="stButton"] > button {
    background-color: #1f77b4;
    color: white;
    border: none;
    font-size: 18px;
    width: 42px;
    height: 42px;
    border-radius: 6px;
}

/* Hover */
.history-toggle div[data-testid="stButton"] > button:hover {
    background-color: #155a8a;
}
</style>
""", unsafe_allow_html=True)
🥈 SECOND → Session state
(Do this once, near the top of your app)
Copy code
Python
if "show_history" not in st.session_state:
    st.session_state.show_history = False
🥉 THIRD → Blue toggle button
Now Streamlit renders the button using the CSS above 👇
Copy code
Python
st.markdown('<div class="history-toggle">', unsafe_allow_html=True)

if st.button("☰", key="history_toggle"):
    st.session_state.show_history = not st.session_state.show_history
    st.rerun()

st.markdown('</div>', unsafe_allow_html=True)
